    "https://www.augie.edu/student-affairs/dean-students-office": {
      "title": "Dean of Students Office",
      "description": "Dean of Students | Augustana University Skip to main content Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Viking Bold Give Careers REQUEST INFO | Search This visually opens the search form. This visually closes the search form. Academics Academics Undergraduate Programs Graduate Programs Academic Calendar Academic Catalog Continuing Education & Workshops Core Curriculum Honor Societies Undergraduate Research Office of Academic Affairs Mikkelsen Library Registrar Student Success Center College of Arts & Sciences Rydell School of Business School of Health Professions School of Music Sharon Lust School of Education Admission & Financial Aid Admission & Financial Aid Admission Counselors Admission Requirements Financial Aid, Costs & Scholarships Test-Optional Admission Admitted Students International Students Transfer Students Global Engagement Global Engagement Prospective International Students Admitted International Students Current International Students Partnerships & Customized Programs Study Abroad Support Global Engagement Student Affairs Student Affairs Accessibility Services Business Office Campus Safety Dean of Students Dining Services Health & Counseling Housing & Residence Life Office of Faith & Spiritual Life Recreational Services Student Engagement Athletics About About About Sioux Falls History Leadership Mission, Vision & Values News Constitution Day Resources Resources Art Galleries & Exhibits Augustana Research Institute Camps & Lessons Campus Learning Center Conferences & Scheduling Directory Events Calendar Office of Advancement Office of Human Resources Theatre Performances VISIT APPLY Dean of Students Office Breadcrumb Home Student Affairs Dean of Students Office Dean of Students Office at AU The Augustana University Dean of Students Office is a resource for students and the campus community that facilitates the integration of academics with all aspects of the university and student life. Personnel in this office are committed to promoting enlightened citizenship, respect for the whole community and the development of healthy lifestyles. The office facilitates interactions among students, faculty and staff to promote a campus climate that supports students' academic success and their personal and professional development. The office is committed to students’ holistic development through delivering innovative programs and services that are responsive to students’ needs, addressing emerging policy issues and fostering community building. The Augustana Dean of Students Office builds a community enriched by diversity and sustained by the university’s core values , civility and mutual respect. Well-Being Communications Form Meet the Dean of Students Beth Elam joined Augustana in 2009 as a graduate assistant residence hall director in the Department of Residence Life. In 2011, Elam stepped into the role of assistant dean of students, overseeing the areas of student health & counseling, supporting students of concern and crisis response. In 2014, she added the role of Title IX coordinator, overseeing the institution's Title IX program. In 2023, Elam began serving as acting dean of students, Elam oversees all aspects of the student experience, including the Dean of Students Office, Augustana Recreational Services, Residence Life and the Division of Student Affairs. Demonstrating outstanding leadership, she was named the dean of students in March 2025. STUDENT CONDUCT STUDENT HANDBOOK REPORT AN INCIDENT TITLE IX POLICIES STUDENT EMERGENCY FUND SPEECH & EXPRESSION SPEAKER POLICY Contact Us 605.274.4124 Dean of Students Office Email Address Augustana University Dean of Students Office Edith Mortenson Center #116 2112 S. Grange Avenue Sioux Falls, SD 57197 Social | | Latest News Five Augustana Students Honored With 2026 Covenant Awards Five Augustana University students received Covenant Awards on Thursday, April 30, during a celebration in Hamre Recital Hall. The Covenant Awards lift up those who exemplify Augustana’s core values: Christian, Liberal Arts, Excellence, Community and Service. Meet the 2026 Covenant Award winners. Augustana University Spring 2025 Dean’s List Recognizes 926 Students Augustana University announced the students who have been named to the Dean's List for the spring semester of the 2024-25 academic year. Congratulations to these 926 students on their academic performance. Shaik, Jancikova Make AU History as First International Student Pair to be Crowned Viking Days Royals Augustana University students Azam Shaik ‘25 and Gabi Jancikova ‘25 were crowned the 2024 Viking Days Royals at coronation on Wednesday, Oct. 2, in the Elmen Center. This is the first time in Augustana’s history that both royals are international students. show more 2001 S. Summit Avenue Sioux Falls, South Dakota 57197 605.274.0770 605.274.0770 800.727.2844 800.727.2844 Explore Academics Admission & Financial Aid Global Engagement Student Affairs Athletics About Resources News Directory AU Merchandise Campus Safety Center for Western Studies Library Connect Current Students Faculty & Staff Alumni Give Careers Search augie.edu Search Apply to Augustana Visit Augustana Augustana University is committed to providing equal access to and participation in employment opportunities, programs and services, without regard to race, color, religion, creed, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, national origin, ancestry, age, veteran status, or disability. Augustana complies with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act, the Americans with Disabilities Act, Rehabilitation Act and other applicable laws providing for nondiscrimination against all individuals. AU will provide reasonable accommodations for known disabilities to the extent required by law. © 2026 Augustana University · All rights reserved. Accessibility Statement Consumer Disclosures Complaints & Concerns FCC File Freedom of Speech & Expression Privacy Policy RSS"
