    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&type=JS&lang=en_US&selectedMenuKey=CurrentOpenings&jobId=557885": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Current Openings | Recruitment Join Our Talent Community Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering Full-Time Faculty Sioux Falls, SD, US 14 days ago Requisition ID: 1400 Apply Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering (start fall 2027) Reports To: Program Director of Engineering, Dr. Carl Olimb Position Summary The Associate Professor of Electrical Engineering is a tenure-track faculty position responsible for teaching undergraduate courses and laboratories in electrical engineering and related areas within the B.S. in Engineering program. The faculty member will contribute to curriculum development, lecture and laboratory instruction, and student design projects while supporting the growth of a new engineering program seeking ABET accreditation within a liberal arts environment. The position includes responsibilities in teaching, scholarship, and service consistent with the expectations of faculty at Augustana University. The faculty member will contribute to the development of an ABET-aligned engineering curriculum and will participate in program assessment and continuous improvement activities. Primary Responsibilities Teaching Teach and create undergraduate courses and laboratories in electrical engineering and related areas such as circuits, electronics, digital systems, or instrumentation. Contribute to introductory engineering and interdisciplinary engineering courses as needed. Develop and implement laboratory experiences that support hands-on engineering education. Mentor undergraduate students in design projects, including capstone design experiences. Advise undergraduate students in the engineering program. Program Development and Assessment Contribute to the development and implementation of the engineering curriculum. Participate in program assessment and continuous improvement activities consistent with ABET accreditation standards. Assist with development of laboratory infrastructure and instructional equipment for electrical engineering coursework with the intent of ABET accreditation. Scholarship Maintain a habit of scholarship according to Augustana’s tenure expectations. Engage undergraduate students in research, design, or applied engineering projects. Service Participate in service activities within the department, college, university, and broader professional community. Contribute to outreach and engagement with regional industry and community partners related to engineering education. Support activities that strengthen the engineering program and its connections to the liberal arts. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering or a closely related engineering discipline. Academic or industry experience aligned with appointment at the Associate level. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate electrical engineering courses. Ability to contribute to laboratory-based and project-based engineering instruction. Effective written and oral communication skills. Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration within a liberal arts environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching in an undergraduate-focused institution. Experience developing or teaching engineering laboratory courses. Experience mentoring undergraduate research or design projects. Experience in preparing for/maintaining ABET accreditation Application Procedure: Full consideration will be given to all complete applications received by 11/18/2026.  For full consideration, please submit the following materials electronically to our Career Center Portal . If assistance is needed during the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu . Application Materials: Curriculum vitae Cover letter Statement of teaching and research interests Three letters of reference Augustana University is an Equal Employment Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence Set your preferences Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below: Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
