    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=026eaaee-2102-4004-840c-8e8ad42d78b1&ccId=19000101_000001&type=JS&lang=en_US&jobId=558345": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Social Work",
      "description": "Current Openings | Recruitment Join Our Talent Community Facebook LinkedIn Email X Copy URL If you are unable to complete this application due to a disability, contact this employer to ask for an accommodation or an alternative application process. Assistant Professor, Social Work Full-Time Faculty Main Campus, Sioux Falls, SD, US 4 days ago Requisition ID: 1407 Apply Position Title: MSW Program faculty, Assistant Professor of Social Work Position Type: Full-Time Department: Social Work Augustana University invites applications for a MSW Program faculty at an Assistant Professor level, beginning Fall 2027 to assist in the development of our new MSW students. Major Areas of Responsibility: The ideal candidate will demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching future social workers in the MSW program actively participating in curriculum design and development and review for the new MSW program work with the MSW Program leadership in fulfilling the program’s mission and goals enhance graduate student experience by serving as academic and career advisor during their time at Augustana University and entry into professional practice. maintain compliance with CSWE standards for explicit/implicit curriculum, field placement, and assessment Augustana prides itself on excellent in-person classroom instruction, thus the successful applicant will demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring students in a liberal arts environment. Required Qualifications: an MSW from a CSWE accredited school required a doctorate in social work or a closely related field required at least two years of post-MSW professional experience high degree of interest, ability and/or experience promoting cultural competency & diversity Preferred Qualifications: doctorate degree in Social Work or related discipline successful teaching experience in social work education Interacting with students, faculty, and administration with different backgrounds and points of view and a deep appreciation of and respect for academic values and shared governance must be top values of the candidate. Location: Augustana’s location in Sioux Falls, South Dakota (www.siouxfalls.com) provides an exceptionally high quality of living in an affordable community environment. Sioux Falls has more than 70 parks, over 40 miles of greenways, a walkable downtown that features musical and cultural events, and award-winning restaurants. Our metro area (population 315,000) is one of the fastest growing regions in the country and is recognized as a major medical, retail, and financial center. If you are looking for a rewarding and dynamic career, look no further than Augustana University in Sioux Falls, SD. Benefits: Augustana offers an excellent benefit package including health insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, AD&D, short- and long-term disability, retirement plan, tuition assistance, holiday, vacation and sick pay. Application Procedure: Interested applicants are asked to submit the application materials listed below in one document to our career center portal. If assistance is needed in the application process, please reach out to humanresources@augie.edu. Official website: augie.edu . a cover letter a statement of teaching philosophy copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts a curriculum vita list of 3 references Augustana University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action/Title IX Employer. Applicants must comply with the Immigration Reform and Control Act and may be required to submit official transcripts upon employment. Finalist candidates must satisfactorily complete a pre-employment background check. Back Apply Copyright © 2026, ADP, Inc. All rights reserved. Powered by Privacy | Legal | Requirements | Artificial Intelligence To manage your preferences, click here Powered by Please switch to a supported browser listed here ,\n      or some features may not work correctly. Our site uses cookies and similar technologies to remember your visit, collect statistics of visits and tailor our site to your interests. They also enable to offer tailored advertising and to link to social networks. For more information or to set your cookie preferences, you may at any time use our tool « Cookie Preferences » at the bottom of our site. Cookie Privacy Statement Set your preferences Deny Agree and proceed Opt-Out Request Honored Set your cookie preferences ADP values your privacy. We provide you with this intuitive tool to help you understand what information may be collected by cookies, by whom, what cookies are used for and to give you control over how the information is being collected and used. For more information on our data policies, please visit our Privacy Statement.\n\nPlease choose whether this site may use Functional, Analytics and/or Advertising cookies, as described below: Select All Required Always Active These cookies are required to enable core site functionality. Functional Functional These cookies are used to enable enhanced functionality and personalization features. Analytics Analytics These cookies allow us to analyze site usage so we can measure and improve performance. Advertising Advertising These cookies are used by advertising companies to serve ads that are relevant to your interests. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Unselect All Save Changes"
